      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to multiply 427 by 412. To make the calculation easier, I'll break down 412 into 400 and 12.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 427 by 400, which gives me 170,800.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 427 by 12, resulting in 5,124.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together: 170,800 plus 5,124 equals 175,924.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **427** and **412**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Breakdown the Multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   427 \\times 412 = 427 \\times (400 + 12) = (427 \\times 400) + (427 \\times 12)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate Each Part Separately:**\n   \n   - **First Part:**\n     \\[\n     427 \\times 400 = 170,\\!800\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Second Part:**\n     \\[\n     427 \\times 12 = 5,\\!124\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the Two Results Together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   170,\\!800 + 5,\\!124 = 175,\\!924\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{175,\\!924}\n   \\]",
