      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to multiply 744 by 841. To make the calculation easier, I'll break down 841 into 800 and 41.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 744 by 800. Multiplying 744 by 800 is the same as multiplying 744 by 8 and then adding three zeros at the end. This gives me 5,952,000.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 744 by 41. I'll break this down further into 744 multiplied by 40 and 744 multiplied by 1. Multiplying 744 by 40 gives me 29,760, and multiplying 744 by 1 gives me 744.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together: 5,952,000 plus 29,760 plus 744 equals 5,982,504.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **744** and **841**, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   744 \\times 841 = 744 \\times (800 + 40 + 1)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 744 by each part separately:**\n\n   - **Multiply by 800:**\n     \\[\n     744 \\times 800 = 744 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 5,952 \\times 100 = 595,200\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 40:**\n     \\[\n     744 \\times 40 = 744 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 2,976 \\times 10 = 29,760\n     \\]\n   \n   - **Multiply by 1:**\n     \\[\n     744 \\times 1 = 744\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add all the results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   595,200 + 29,760 + 744 = 595,200 + 30,504 = 625,704\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n   \n   \\[\n   \\boxed{625704}\n   \\]",
      "logprobs": null,
