      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to multiply 564 by 111. To simplify the calculation, I can break down 111 into 100 + 10 + 1.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 564 by each of these components separately.\n\nStarting with 564 multiplied by 100, I'll add two zeros to 564, resulting in 56,400.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 564 by 10, which is straightforward and gives me 5,640.\n\nFinally, I'll multiply 564 by 1, which is simply 564.\n\nAfter obtaining all three products, I'll add them together: 56,400 + 5,640 + 564.\n\nAdding these numbers step by step, I first add 56,400 and 5,640 to get 62,040, and then add 564 to reach the final product of 62,604.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of 564 and 111, we can use the distributive property of multiplication.\n\n\\[\n564 \\times 111 = 564 \\times (100 + 10 + 1)\n\\]\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n1. **Multiply 564 by 100:**\n   \\[\n   564 \\times 100 = 56,\\!400\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 564 by 10:**\n   \\[\n   564 \\times 10 = 5,\\!640\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 564 by 1:**\n   \\[\n   564 \\times 1 = 564\n   \\]\n\nNow, add all the results together:\n\n\\[\n56,\\!400 + 5,\\!640 + 564 = 62,\\!604\n\\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{62,\\!604}\n\\]",
      "logprobs": null,
      "finish_reason": "stop",
      "stop_reason": null,
      "prompt_logprobs": null
    }
  ],
