      "text": "<think>\nFirst, I need to multiply 569 by 714. To make this easier, I'll break down 714 into 700 and 14.\n\nNext, I'll multiply 569 by 700. Multiplying by 700 is the same as multiplying by 7 and then adding two zeros. So, 569 multiplied by 7 is 4,083, and adding two zeros gives me 408,300.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 569 by 14. I'll start by multiplying 569 by 10, which is 5,690, and then multiply 569 by 4, which is 2,276. Adding these two results together gives me 7,966.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two partial products, 408,300 and 7,966, to get the final answer of 416,266.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 569 and 714, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   569 \\times 714 = 569 \\times (700 + 14) = 569 \\times 700 + 569 \\times 14\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n\n   - **First part: \\(569 \\times 700\\)**\n     \n     \\[\n     569 \\times 700 = 569 \\times 7 \\times 100 = 4,083 \\times 100 = 408,300\n     \\]\n     \n   - **Second part: \\(569 \\times 14\\)**\n     \n     \\[\n     569 \\times 14 = (500 \\times 14) + (69 \\times 14) = 7,000 + 966 = 7,966\n     \\]\n\n3. **Add the two results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   408,300 + 7,966 = 416,266\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{416266}\n\\]",
